                        "entry_id": "b91015a7-32d0-3bca-9a6f-cb7207d224c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Whatever person or persons (as object of verb or preposition)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37f645bb-b4ae-4fc0-99e3-5a68090b40e5",
                                "sense_id": "57f5bd8b-3356-352a-bf75-c988988f10fd",
                                "text": "The letter is addressed to whomever it may concern."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0799fbb-611e-40d6-8f3b-51a0413f2d85",
                                "sense_id": "57f5bd8b-3356-352a-bf75-c988988f10fd",
                                "text": "I'll marry whomever I want."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "986abf3a-2dd1-46c9-ae95-4a95ac08aa2b",
                                "sense_id": "57f5bd8b-3356-352a-bf75-c988988f10fd",
                                "text": "To impose his will on whomever he sees comfortably settled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7a35151-5e07-40c0-b446-472ff00d9f87",
                                "sense_id": "57f5bd8b-3356-352a-bf75-c988988f10fd",
                                "text": "Yes, the tide will surely turn, and meanwhile may one who is proud to call himself a partisan, invite whomever may feel disposed to bid the \"T14s\" adieux, to pause before giving them valediction and accord to them the respect that is assuredly their due."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
